    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T23:22:02Z",
    "body": "Found in the reporter's first working session (v0.26.0, Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, 2026-11-23):\n1. **Failed turns are re-sent.** The earlier messages that failed (no key) stayed in the conversation. When \"hi\" finally went through, the model received all of them. It acted on the old failed \"create a facing operation\" request and added Face1. Its reply says: \"The message \"hi\" came through several times. I treated them all as one request.\" A failed turn must not be replayed. Either drop it from the history, or send it again only when the user presses Retry on it. A chat that changes the project should act only on what the user sent in this turn.\n2. **Markdown is shown raw.** Replies show `**Face1**` and `- **Tool:**` literally. Render bold and lists, or ask the model for plain text.\n3. Keep: the \"2 changes in this turn · Undo Turn\" row worked and is clear.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
