    "body": "More from the reporter's session (2026-11-23):\n4. **Tool calls are dumped as raw JSON in the conversation.** A `get_job` call shows its whole answer inline: setup, machine, model bounds, the model's file path. That buries the reply. Show each tool call as one collapsed line, for example \"get_job ✓ · show details\". Expand it on click, and have a panel setting \"Show tool details\" (off by default) for debugging. Keep errors visible: show a failed call expanded, with its message.\n5. **Privacy note for the getting-started message.** That JSON includes the full local path of the model file (`/Users/<name>/...`), and it goes to the cloud provider. Say in the getting-started text what the assistant sends. Consider sending only the file name.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
